Jahshaka local patch 0033 (upstream-reportable): a CASCADE CHAIN loses the
ambient. Every surface the bounce does not reach renders BLACK instead of
ambient-lit, and the loss compounds once per cascade.

Measured on `gi.cascades` case 4 — a ground lit by NOTHING but a flat ambient,
Epic, the Ogre sample's four-cascade set — as a fraction of the same ground with
GI off (the single scene-fitted volume and a chain of ONE cascade both read
1.00x, so neither the ambient push nor the cascade placement is at fault):

    chain length              1       2       3       4
    shipped media             -       -       -     0.00x   (black)
    fix 1, escape line only   -       -       -     0.02x
    fix 1, both lines       1.00x   0.61x   0.27x   0.16x
    fix 1 + fix 2           1.00x   0.75x   0.56x   0.51x

(A dash is a combination that was not measured; the two sweeps were.)

FIX 1 — TWO ACCUMULATORS THAT DOUBLE AT EVERY HOP. `voxelConeTraceDiff` starts
both of its accumulators at the alpha it is handed (`float alpha = startingAlpha;`
upstream, `float escapeAlpha = startingAlpha;` Jahshaka patch 0021), and that
argument is the caller's own `result.alpha` — so what the call RETURNS is already
the running total for the whole cone. The cascade continuation loop then ADDED
those totals to the values it already held:

    result.alpha       += newRes.alpha;          // upstream's
    result.escapeAlpha += newRes.escapeAlpha;    // patch 0021's, same shape

Both opacities therefore double per hop: the walk exits early through
`result.alpha < 0.95f` so the outer cascades are never gathered from, and —
because the doubled alpha is what seeds the next call's escapeAlpha —
`1 - min(1, escapeAlpha / 0.95)`, the weight the ambient rides on (`light.w`,
`light.xyz += ambient * light.w`), reaches exactly 0 after three hops. Fix:
assign, because the returned value IS the running total. The colour composite on
the line above deliberately reads the PREVIOUS `result.alpha` (upstream's
de-amplification of the coarser cascade, `VctCascadedVoxelizer::update`'s own
comment) and is evaluated before either assignment, so it is unchanged.

FIX 2 — THE SELF-OCCLUSION BIAS IS APPLIED ONCE, NOT ONCE PER CASCADE.
`computeVctProbe` starts the cone one bias away from the surface it stands on
(`posLS += (dirLS / maxVal) * vctInvResolution * lerp( 15.0f, 1.0f, maxVal )`),
which is what stops a floor occluding its own cone. The continuation into the
next cascade re-enters at the point the previous march stopped — about two of
the PREVIOUS cascade's voxels above the floor, i.e. inside one cell of the
coarser one — and applies no such bias at all (it moves BACKWARD by one voxel,
`- dir * startBias`, to avoid a gap at the seam). So every cascade samples the
starting surface again, at its own coarser mip, and the escape opacity climbs a
step per hop. Fix: apply the same expression the initial call uses, in the NEW
cascade's units, at every cascade entry.

AMENDED 2026-09-14 (PHOTON E0, audit B5) — THE SAME TWO FIXES ON THE SPECULAR
WALK. The first version of this patch fixed the DIFFUSE cone loop only. The
cascade continuation is run twice per pixel, and the specular one (the sky in a
reflection) carried both defects unchanged: `irrLight.alpha += newRes.alpha`
(the same doubling, `voxelConeTraceSpec` also starts its accumulator at the
`startingAlpha` it is handed) and no self-occlusion bias at the new cascade's
entry. So once the inner cascade's opacity reached 0.475 the doubled total
crossed the walk's own `< 0.95f` exit after ONE hop and
`specAlpha = 1 - min( 1, alpha / 0.95 )` was 0 — the ambient term in the
specular result vanished at 2+ cascades. Measured on a chrome plate lit by
nothing but the ambient, `gi.cascades` case 7 (mean luminance of the plate):

    roughness      0.15     0.35     0.55     0.75
    1 cascade    0.0264   0.0036   0.0019   0.0039   (the reference)
    2 cascades   0.0148   0.0000   0.0000   0.0000   before this amendment
    4 cascades   0.0001   0.0000   0.0000   0.0000   before this amendment

The bias term differs from the diffuse one in one detail, and deliberately:
`startBias` in the specular loop measures the new cascade's voxel along the
REFLECTION ray (it is upstream's seam-gap term and stays as it is), while the
self-occlusion bias must be along the GEOMETRIC NORMAL — so the amendment
computes `normalBias` in the new cascade's units, which is exactly what
`computeVctProbe`'s initial `vctInvResolution` is for cascade 0.

IT IS AN AMENDMENT, NOT A NEW PATCH: the number stays 0033, because the two
halves are one fix to one defect and a tree that carries the old 0033 and not
this one is in a state nobody should have to reason about. A tree that already
applied the old 0033 must reset the file (`git checkout -- Samples/Media` in the
ogre-next submodule + the usual `clean -fd`) before re-running build-ogre.sh.

RESIDUAL, STATED HONESTLY: 0.51x at four cascades, not 1.00x. The rest is
upstream's march bookkeeping — `voxelConeTraceDiff` RESTARTS `dist` at one voxel
in each cascade (`float dist = vctInvResolution;`) instead of carrying the
distance the cone has already travelled, so the continuation re-marches the near
field with a footprint computed for a cone one voxel long. Carrying the travelled
distance across the hop (a `VctResult::dist` scaled by
`fromPreviousProbeToNext[j-1][0].xyz`) is the real fix and it is a bigger change
than this patch: recorded for SPECS/OGRE_UPSTREAM_ISSUES.md and for PHOTON P1.
It is bounded: with the irradiance field on, the field REPLACES the cone diffuse
(`vct_disable_diffuse`), so this term only lights tiers that run without it.

NO EXISTING PICTURE CAN MOVE. Both hunks are inside `@property( vct_num_probes >
1 )`, which is only true when a cascade CHAIN is bound, and nothing in this tree
builds one except Photon's arm (`GiParams::cascades`, off by default and off in
every shipped scene). Verified: the `--engine-selftest` hash is byte-identical
with the patch staged.

MEDIA-ONLY (Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Vct_piece_ps.any): no Ogre rebuild, but
every tree must run the patch loop — Studio stages Hlms media from the SOURCE
tree. Applies after patch 0021, whose line fix 1 corrects. Verified with
`git apply --check` against the patched-through-0032 tree and
`git apply --reverse --check` after applying. Rationale also in
irisgl/docs/OGRE_BUILD.md, entry 33.

